export const docsContent: Record<string, string> = {
  "get-started/introduction": "# Introduction\n\nPraxis Skills is a **Codex-first**, agent-portable package of engineering workflows. It takes product and engineering work from an unclear request to a reviewed implementation and pull request.\n\nEvery phase writes **inspectable files**. The package does not depend on hidden orchestration or chat memory alone.\n\n## What you get\n\n- Reusable skills for init, refine, research, design, plan, implement, docs, QA, Sentry triage, and PR\n- Project direction that survives the session (`.praxis/project.md`)\n- Resumable feature state under `.workflows/{feature-id}/`\n- Multi-agent install maps for Codex, Claude Code, Cursor, and Grok\n- Optional Taste Skill full-family install (default off)\n- Human checkpoints at direction, design, and ship\n\n## Design principles\n\n| Principle | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| Artifact-driven | Decisions and evidence live in the repository |\n| Complexity-adaptive | Small work can take a short path; large work keeps ceremony |\n| Human-supervised | Costly steps wait for confirmation when the skill contracts say so |\n| Portable knowledge | `SKILL.md` + Markdown references, not a closed runtime API |\n| Codex-primary | Codex is maintained and verified; other agents are best-effort |\n\n## What Praxis is not\n\n- Not a hosted orchestration SaaS\n- Not a hard kernel that can force an LLM to obey checkpoints\n- Not a full enterprise approval product with roles and queues\n- Not a guarantee of multi-agent feature parity without testing\n\n## Runtime support\n\n| Surface | Portability |\n|---|---|\n| `SKILL.md` and Markdown references | Agent-portable in principle |\n| `.praxis/project.md`, `.praxis/skills.yaml` | Plain files any capable agent can read |\n| `.workflows/{id}/` | Runtime-independent evidence and resume state |\n| `.agents/skills` discovery | Primary Codex layout |\n| Claude slash adapters | `/praxis-*` only where installed |\n| MCP tool names | Environment-specific; degrade when missing |\n\n**Codex** is the primary, actively verified target. Other skill-capable agents get best-effort portability.\n\n## Next\n\n- [Installation](/docs/get-started/installation)\n- [Quick start](/docs/get-started/quick-start)\n- [Architecture](/docs/concepts/architecture)\n",
  "get-started/installation": "# Installation\n\n## Requirements\n\n- Node.js **22+** for the npm installer\n- Git for history-aware workflows\n- Python 3 for project profile validation\n- A coding agent that can load skills and repository files (Codex primary)\n- PowerShell 7 (Windows) or Bash (macOS/Linux) only for checkout fallback scripts\n\nOptional: Sentry, Context7, and documentation MCP servers. Workflows degrade when they are absent.\n\n## Recommended: npm (beta channel)\n\nThe release channel is **beta**. Pin the tag so `npx` selects the newest prerelease.\n\n### Guided install (TTY)\n\n```bash\nnpx praxis-skills@beta install\n```\n\nWalkthrough: scope (user vs repo) → agent checkboxes → optional Taste Skill (default off) → plan → confirm.\n\n### User-global\n\n```bash\nnpx praxis-skills@beta install --user --yes\nnpx praxis-skills@beta doctor --user\n```\n\n### Multi-agent\n\n```bash\nnpx praxis-skills@beta detect\nnpx praxis-skills@beta install --user --agents codex,claude-code --yes\nnpx praxis-skills@beta install --user --all-agents --yes\n```\n\n| Agent id | User skills path | Extra |\n|---|---|---|\n| `codex` | `~/.agents/skills` | Primary discovery |\n| `claude-code` | `~/.claude/skills` | Slash adapters `/praxis-*` under `commands/` |\n| `cursor` | `~/.cursor/skills` | Cursor Agent Skills |\n| `grok` | `~/.grok/skills` | Grok Build skills |\n\n### Repository install\n\n```bash\nnpx praxis-skills@beta install --repo . --agents codex,claude-code --yes\n```\n\n- Codex / Grok → `.agents/skills`\n- Claude Code → `.claude/skills` + `.claude/commands`\n- Cursor → `.cursor/skills`\n\n### Taste Skill (optional)\n\n```bash\nnpx praxis-skills@beta install --user --with-taste-skill --yes\n```\n\nInstalls the **full** Taste Skill family at the revision pinned in `distribution/taste-skill.json`. Default is **off**. See [Taste Skill routing](/docs/concepts/taste-skill) and [CLI Taste flag](/docs/cli/taste-skill).\n\n### Useful flags\n\n| Flag | Purpose |\n|---|---|\n| `--user` / `--repo [path]` / `--target <dir>` | Install scope |\n| `--agents id,id` / `--all-agents` | Agent targets |\n| `--with-taste-skill` / `--no-taste-skill` | Optional Taste family |\n| `--force` | Replace existing Praxis-owned skills |\n| `--yes` | Non-interactive confirm |\n| `--dry-run` | Plan only |\n| `--json` | Machine-readable output |\n| `--with-slash-commands` / `--no-slash-commands` | Claude adapters |\n\n### After install\n\nRestart the agent session so the skill catalog refreshes.\n\n```bash\nnpx praxis-skills@beta doctor --user --agents codex,claude-code\nnpx praxis-skills@beta list\nnpx praxis-skills@beta version\n```\n\n## Checkout fallback\n\nWhen Node is unavailable, clone the repository and use install scripts:\n\n```powershell\ngit clone https://github.com/EdwyReed/praxis-skills.git\ncd praxis-skills\npwsh ./install.ps1 --user --force\npwsh ./verify-install.ps1\n```\n\nOn macOS/Linux: `./install.sh --user --force`.\n\n## Plugin install (source checkout)\n\nThe plugin bundle lives in `plugin/` (`.codex-plugin/plugin.json` + packaged skills).\n\n```powershell\npwsh ./install.ps1 --plugin --dry-run\npwsh ./install.ps1 --plugin\npwsh ./verify-install.ps1\n```\n\nWrites a local marketplace entry under `.agents/plugins/marketplace.json` for repo-local testing.\n\nSource:\n\n- [docs/how/install-as-plugin.md](https://github.com/EdwyReed/praxis-skills/blob/master/docs/how/install-as-plugin.md)\n- [docs/how/install.md](https://github.com/EdwyReed/praxis-skills/blob/master/docs/how/install.md)\n\n## Uninstall\n\n```bash\nnpx praxis-skills@beta uninstall --user --agents claude-code --yes\nnpx praxis-skills@beta uninstall --user --dry-run\n```\n\nOnly manifest-owned Praxis paths are removed. Unrelated skills stay.\n\nMore detail: [docs/how/uninstall.md](https://github.com/EdwyReed/praxis-skills/blob/master/docs/how/uninstall.md)\n\n## Next\n\n- [Quick start](/docs/get-started/quick-start)\n- [CLI install reference](/docs/cli/install)\n",
  "get-started/quick-start": "# Quick start\n\n## 1. Install\n\n```bash\nnpx praxis-skills@beta install --user --yes\n```\n\nRestart your agent (Codex recommended).\n\n## 2. Open a repository\n\nIn the target project:\n\n```text\nUse $praxis-init to audit this repository and initialize Praxis project context.\n```\n\nReview `.praxis/project.md`. Correct it. Confirm it. Until status is confirmed, agents should not treat inferred direction as final.\n\n## 3. Run a feature flow (or a single skill)\n\nFull lifecycle:\n\n```text\nUse $praxis-feature-flow for account recovery.\n```\n\nOr one phase:\n\n```text\nUse $praxis-research to find how report totals are calculated. Facts only.\nUse $praxis-design for the approved notification change.\nUse $praxis-qa-checklist for checkout with coupons.\n```\n\n## 4. Inspect artifacts\n\n| Path | Role |\n|---|---|\n| `.praxis/project.md` | Confirmed project direction |\n| `.praxis/skills.yaml` | Optional external skill pins |\n| `.workflows/{feature-id}/` | Phase evidence and `state.json` |\n| Root `AGENTS.md` | Discovery bridge block |\n\n## 5. Human gates\n\n| Gate | When |\n|---|---|\n| Direction | After init draft |\n| Design | Before large implementation |\n| Ship | Before merge |\n\nSee [Human checkpoints](/docs/concepts/human-checkpoints).\n\n## Claude Code\n\nIf you installed `claude-code`:\n\n- Skills: `~/.claude/skills/praxis-*`\n- Commands: `/praxis-init`, `/praxis-feature`, `/praxis-research`, …\n\nPrefix avoids collision with Claude built-in `/init`.\n\n## Next\n\n- [Feature flow overview](/docs/flow/overview)\n- [Skills catalog](/docs/skills/catalog)\n",
  "get-started/agents": "# Agents\n\nPraxis installs into agent-specific skill homes. Workflow **semantics** stay in `SKILL.md`. Only discovery paths and thin adapters differ.\n\n## Supported install targets\n\n| Id | User skills | Repo skills | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `codex` | `~/.agents/skills` | `.agents/skills` | Primary, verified |\n| `claude-code` | `~/.claude/skills` | `.claude/skills` | Plus `/praxis-*` slash adapters |\n| `cursor` | `~/.cursor/skills` | `.cursor/skills` | Best-effort |\n| `grok` | `~/.grok/skills` | `.agents/skills` or mapped home | Best-effort |\n\nDetect without install:\n\n```bash\nnpx praxis-skills@beta detect\nnpx praxis-skills@beta detect --json\n```\n\n## Codex\n\nCodex loads skills from user and repo `.agents/skills` trees and honors repository `AGENTS.md` when configured.\n\nInvoke explicitly:\n\n```text\nUse $praxis-init …\nUse $praxis-feature-flow …\n```\n\n## Claude Code\n\nInstall:\n\n```bash\nnpx praxis-skills@beta install --user --agents claude-code --yes\n```\n\nYou get:\n\n1. Skill packages under skills home  \n2. Slash command files that **load** Praxis skills (no forked logic)\n\nExamples: `/praxis-init`, `/praxis-feature`, `/praxis-research`, `/praxis-design`.\n\nLegacy unprefixed command files are removed on install when Praxis owns them.\n\n## Cursor and Grok\n\nSkills are copied into the agent skill directory. Invocation depends on that agent's skill loader. Treat as best-effort until you verify in your environment.\n\n## Portability rules\n\n1. Do not fork workflow text into agent-specific command bodies  \n2. Keep runtime packaging separate from workflow contracts  \n3. Accept compatibility only after real use in that agent  \n\n## Next\n\n- [Architecture](/docs/concepts/architecture)\n- [Installation](/docs/get-started/installation)\n",
  "concepts/architecture": "# Architecture\n\n## Layers\n\n```text\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  Agent runtime (Codex, Claude, Cursor, …)   │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│  Discovery: skills homes, AGENTS.md, slash  │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│  Praxis skills (SKILL.md + references)      │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│  Project contracts: .praxis/*               │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│  Feature evidence: .workflows/{id}/         │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n## Package layout (source)\n\n| Path | Role |\n|---|---|\n| `.agents/skills/` | Canonical skill packages |\n| `plugin/skills/` | Installable mirror for npm/plugin |\n| `references/` | Shared roles, rules, scenarios, templates |\n| `distribution/manifest.json` | Exact npm payload ownership |\n| `distribution/taste-skill.json` | Taste Skill pin + catalog |\n| `bin/`, `lib/` | Zero-dependency CLI |\n| `docs/` | Maintainer docs in the [package repo](https://github.com/EdwyReed/praxis-skills/blob/master/docs) |\n\n## Source of truth\n\n- **Workflow contracts:** `SKILL.md` under skill packages  \n- **Install ownership:** `distribution/manifest.json`  \n- **Project direction:** `.praxis/project.md` after confirmation  \n- **Feature resume:** `.workflows/{id}/state.json`  \n\nThe CLI copies only manifest-listed skill directories. It does not run lifecycle scripts and does not invent project files on install.\n\n## Subagents\n\nSubagents are optional. Every workflow that can use them also describes an **inline** path.\n\n## Related\n\n- [Project context](/docs/concepts/project-context)\n- [Artifacts](/docs/concepts/artifacts)\n- [Feature flow](/docs/flow/overview)\n",
  "concepts/project-context": "# Project context\n\nRepository-scoped Praxis work starts with `$praxis-init`. It creates two separate contracts.\n\n## `.praxis/project.md` (mandatory)\n\nDurable project direction:\n\n- concept and outcomes  \n- priorities and non-goals  \n- experience qualities (desired / avoid)  \n- one primary visual skill when frontend is in scope, or `none`  \n- references with exact links  \n- technical, accessibility, legal, operational, language constraints  \n- open questions  \n- confirmation state  \n\n### Clear Speech mode\n\nFrontmatter `clear_speech`:\n\n| Value | Behavior |\n|---|---|\n| `default` | Core rules everywhere; English technical profile on technical English |\n| `strict` | English technical profile on all eligible English prose |\n| `off` | No automatic Clear Speech (still invocable per task) |\n\nMissing field → treat as `default`.\n\n### Confirmation\n\nInferred profiles use `status: needs-confirmation`. Repository mutations that depend on direction wait until the user confirms.\n\n### Size limits\n\n- Core Contract ≤ **400** words  \n- Full profile ≤ **2,500** words  \n\nValidator emits SHA-256. Workflows record the digest they used.\n\n## `.praxis/skills.yaml` (optional)\n\nOnly when the project needs **external** nonstandard skill packages to reproduce workflow or design direction.\n\nRules:\n\n- `required` or `recommended` only  \n- one package/family per role  \n- entrypoint skills, not the whole remote catalog  \n- pinned git revisions (no `main` / `latest`)  \n- `applies_when` + rationale  \n- overflow justification after five required packages  \n\nPraxis never auto-installs listed packages. Missing required packages block only the affected work after the agent explains the gap and you decide.\n\n## `AGENTS.md` bridge\n\nInit adds a managed block so Codex (and similar agents) can discover `.praxis/project.md` even when the session is crowded.\n\nSee [AGENTS.md](/docs/config/agents-md).\n\n## Validation\n\n```bash\npython .agents/skills/praxis-init/scripts/validate_project.py .\n```\n\n(or the path inside your install)\n\n## Next\n\n- [project.md reference](/docs/config/project-md)\n- [skills.yaml reference](/docs/config/skills-yaml)\n",
  "concepts/artifacts": "# Artifacts and workflows\n\n## Why files\n\nChat is ephemeral. Agents change. Praxis writes **evidence** you can reopen, review, and resume.\n\n## `.workflows/{feature-id}/`\n\nTypical layout (varies by path taken):\n\n```text\n.workflows/042-account-recovery/\n  state.json\n  refine/\n  research/\n  design/\n  plan/\n  implement/\n  docs/\n  pr/\n  qa/\n```\n\n| Area | Examples |\n|---|---|\n| `state.json` | Phase status, complexity, frontend gate, project hash |\n| `research/` | Facts-only notes, complexity |\n| `design/` | architecture.md, diagrams, ADRs |\n| `plan/` | overview, phase-N.md |\n| `implement/` | phase reports, review notes |\n| `pr/` | summary, test plan links |\n\n## State machine (phases)\n\nAllowed phase states: `pending`, `in_progress`, `done`, `skipped`, `blocked`.\n\nExpected phase keys include: refinement, research, design, design_review, plan, implement, docs, pr (see [state schema](/docs/flow/state)).\n\n## Independence\n\nYou can invoke a single skill without a full feature flow. Feature flow coordinates phases when you want resume and adaptive ceremony.\n\n## Git hygiene\n\nCommit workflow artifacts when they are decisions or evidence the team needs. Do not treat them as disposable temp files if you care about auditability.\n\n## Next\n\n- [Feature flow](/docs/flow/overview)\n- [Human checkpoints](/docs/concepts/human-checkpoints)\n",
  "concepts/human-checkpoints": "# Human checkpoints\n\nPraxis is **human-supervised** through skill contracts and repository files. It is not a hard approval product that can force an LLM click.\n\n## Primary gates\n\n| Gate | Skill | You | Agent |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **Direction** | `$praxis-init` | Confirm or correct `.praxis/project.md` | Drafts profile; waits when status is needs-confirmation |\n| **Design** | `$praxis-design` | Accept, revise, or stop | Writes architecture/ADRs; does not silently jump to code |\n| **Ship** | `$praxis-pr` | Review PR body and evidence; merge is yours | Assembles artifacts; does not invent missing review |\n\n## Additional consent points\n\n- Installing external skills or Taste Skill family  \n- Accepting a **small/fast** path that skips ceremony  \n- Missing required packages in `.praxis/skills.yaml`  \n\n## What files give you\n\nWhile you decide, agents should leave **artifacts** (research, design drafts, open questions) so another session or agent can continue after your answer.\n\n## Limits (honest)\n\n- Checkpoint policy is soft: a session can ignore the skill  \n- No multi-approver roles or SLA queues  \n- Small paths reduce ceremony when you accept them  \n\n## Related\n\n- [Complexity paths](/docs/concepts/complexity)\n- [Feature flow](/docs/flow/overview)\n",
  "concepts/complexity": "# Complexity paths\n\n`$praxis-feature-flow` adjusts ceremony to task size after assessment (and often after you accept the plan).\n\n| Complexity | Typical path |\n|---|---|\n| **Small** | Research → Implement → PR (after you accept fast track) |\n| **Medium** | Focused research; lighter design/plan/review |\n| **Large** | Full refine → research → design → plan → implement → review → docs → PR |\n\n## Rules of thumb\n\n- Prefer **facts before solutions** even on small work  \n- Design remains a **human checkpoint** for non-trivial change  \n- Do not force full ceremony on a one-line fix  \n- Do not skip design on a multi-system redesign without explicit acceptance  \n\n## Recording\n\nComplexity and rationale live in `state.json` so resume does not re-litigate the choice blindly.\n\n## Next\n\n- [Phases](/docs/flow/phases)\n- [Feature flow overview](/docs/flow/overview)\n",
  "concepts/taste-skill": "# Taste Skill routing\n\n[Taste Skill](https://www.tasteskill.dev/) is the recommended visual skill family for marketing surfaces and many redesigns. Praxis **routes** to it. It does **not** ship Taste files inside the default npm payload unless you opt in.\n\n## Core policy\n\n1. **Missing Taste Skill never blocks work**  \n2. **Present applicable skill must be loaded and used**  \n3. **Missing → offer install proactively** (consent required)  \n4. **Exactly one primary visual skill** for art direction  \n5. **Default primary:** `design-taste-frontend` (v2 experimental)\n\n## Pin\n\n`distribution/taste-skill.json` records:\n\n- repository: `https://github.com/Leonxlnx/taste-skill`  \n- revision (git SHA)  \n- channel: `v2-experimental`  \n- full install-name catalog  \n\n## Install with Praxis\n\n```bash\nnpx praxis-skills@beta install --user --with-taste-skill --yes\n```\n\nUpstream single skill:\n\n```bash\nnpx skills add https://github.com/Leonxlnx/taste-skill --skill \"design-taste-frontend\"\n```\n\n## Routing table (install names)\n\n| Task | Primary install name |\n|---|---|\n| Landing / portfolio / marketing | `design-taste-frontend` |\n| Existing UI modernization | `redesign-existing-projects` |\n| Image-first design-to-code | `image-to-code` |\n| Soft / premium agency | `high-end-visual-design` |\n| Minimalist | `minimalist-ui` |\n| Brutalist / industrial | `industrial-brutalist-ui` |\n| Stricter GPT/Codex motion | `gpt-taste` |\n| Google Stitch / DESIGN.md | `stitch-design-taste` |\n| Web / mobile / brand images | `imagegen-frontend-web`, `imagegen-frontend-mobile`, `brandkit` |\n| Legacy v1 | `design-taste-frontend-v1` |\n\n`full-output-enforcement` is a **supplement**, never a primary visual skill.\n\n## Out of scope\n\nDense dashboards, multi-step admin UI, data tables as product, game engines: do **not** force Taste as primary. Prefer repo design systems and technical frontend skills. Record rationale.\n\n## Precedence\n\nUser instructions → repository rules → approved design → routing policy.\n\n## State fields\n\nIn feature `state.json`:\n\n- `frontend.applicable`  \n- `frontend.status`: `not-applicable` | `selected` | `prohibited` | `declined` | `awaiting-install-consent` | `missing-continued`  \n- `frontend.primary_skill`  \n- `frontend.channel`  \n- `frontend.rationale`  \n- `frontend.taste_skill_offered`  \n\n## Next\n\n- [CLI Taste flag](/docs/cli/taste-skill)\n- [Frontend guide](/docs/guides/frontend)\n",
  "concepts/clear-speech": "# Clear Speech\n\nPraxis Clear Speech is an independent writing policy inspired by clear technical writing principles from ASD-STE100 Issue 9.\n\nPraxis does **not** bundle the official standard or dictionary. Results are **not** ASD certification.\n\n## Modes (`clear_speech` in project.md)\n\n| Mode | Behavior |\n|---|---|\n| `default` | Core rules all languages; English technical profile on technical English |\n| `strict` | English technical profile on all eligible English prose |\n| `off` | No automatic application; still invocable as `$praxis-clear-speech` |\n\n## Protected content\n\nDo not rewrite:\n\n- source identifiers and syntax  \n- public API names, fields, protocol values  \n- exact quotes, legal text, trademarks  \n- approved project glossary terms  \n\n## Surfaces\n\n- LLM replies  \n- documentation  \n- UI copy, errors, logs, help  \n- comments and docstrings  \n\n## Audit\n\n```bash\npython .agents/skills/praxis-clear-speech/scripts/audit_text.py <path>\npython .agents/skills/praxis-clear-speech/scripts/audit_text.py <path> --sentence-limit 20\n```\n\nAutomated checks are aids. They do not prove full standard compliance.\n\n## Skill\n\nSee [`$praxis-clear-speech`](/docs/skills/praxis-clear-speech).\n",
  "flow/overview": "# Feature flow overview\n\n`$praxis-feature-flow` (also referred to as feature lifecycle / `$praxis-feature` in some UIs) coordinates complexity-adaptive delivery under `.workflows/{feature-id}/`.\n\n## When to use\n\n- Multi-phase product or engineering change  \n- Need resume/status across sessions  \n- Want adaptive ceremony with checkpoints  \n\n## When not to use\n\n- Single atomic skill is enough (`$praxis-research` alone, etc.)  \n- Pure documentation or QA-only task (use dedicated skills)\n\n## High-level path\n\n```text\ninit (project) → refine → research → design → plan → implement → gates → pr\n                 ↑\n            sentry-triage\n```\n\nIndividual skills remain callable without the orchestrator.\n\n## Responsibilities\n\n1. Ensure project context is confirmed when required  \n2. Assess complexity; propose path  \n3. Run or delegate phases  \n4. Persist `state.json`  \n5. Stop at human checkpoints  \n6. Support resume/status  \n\n## Next\n\n- [Phases](/docs/flow/phases)\n- [State schema](/docs/flow/state)\n- [Resume](/docs/flow/resume)\n",
  "flow/phases": "# Phases\n\nFeature flow phases (names as used in state):\n\n| Phase | Skill / activity | Output |\n|---|---|---|\n| refinement | `$praxis-refine` | Task contract, stories, risks |\n| research | `$praxis-research` | Facts-only research |\n| design | `$praxis-design` | Architecture, ADRs, contracts |\n| design_review | human + reviewers | Acceptance of design |\n| plan | `$praxis-plan` | Vertical phases + verification |\n| implement | `$praxis-implement` | Code + review/gate evidence |\n| docs | `$praxis-docs-suite` | Docs suite updates |\n| pr | `$praxis-pr` | PR from artifacts |\n\nSupporting intakes:\n\n| Intake | Skill |\n|---|---|\n| Sentry | `$praxis-sentry-triage` → refine/feature |\n| QA-only | `$praxis-qa-checklist` |\n| System map | `$praxis-system-profile` |\n\n## Design checkpoint\n\nPraxis must not silently move from inferred design into implementation. Large changes keep an explicit design review step.\n\n## Implementation granularity\n\nImplement **one planned phase** at a time unless you explicitly widen scope.\n\n## Next\n\n- [State schema](/docs/flow/state)\n- [Skills catalog](/docs/skills/catalog)\n",
  "flow/state": "# State schema\n\nFile: `.workflows/{feature-id}/state.json`\n\n## Required keys\n\n| Key | Type |\n|---|---|\n| `feature_id` | string |\n| `source` | string or null |\n| `complexity` | `small` \\| `medium` \\| `large` \\| null |\n| `complexity_reason` | string or null |\n| `phases` | object keyed by phase name |\n| `project_context.status` | `needs-confirmation` \\| `confirmed` |\n| `project_context.profile_sha256` | string |\n| `project_context.skills_manifest_sha256` | string or null |\n| `project_context.validated_at` | ISO datetime |\n\n## Phase states\n\n`pending` · `in_progress` · `done` · `skipped` · `blocked`\n\n## Frontend gate (optional)\n\n| Field | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| `frontend.applicable` | boolean |\n| `frontend.status` | `not-applicable` \\| `selected` \\| `prohibited` \\| `declined` \\| `awaiting-install-consent` \\| `missing-continued` |\n| `frontend.primary_skill` | install name or null |\n| `frontend.channel` | e.g. `v2-experimental` |\n| `frontend.rationale` | short string |\n| `frontend.taste_skill_offered` | boolean |\n\n## Expected phase keys\n\nrefinement · research · design · design_review · plan · implement · docs · pr\n\n## Integrity\n\nWhen the project profile hash changes, re-validate context before continuing mutations that depend on direction.\n",
  "flow/resume": "# Resume and status\n\n## Status\n\nAsk the agent:\n\n```text\nUse $praxis-feature-flow to report status for 042-account-recovery.\n```\n\nExpected answer: complexity, phase table, blockers, next human decision.\n\n## Resume\n\n```text\nResume $praxis-feature-flow for 042-account-recovery from the current state.\n```\n\nAgent should:\n\n1. Read `state.json`  \n2. Re-read project profile hash  \n3. Continue the next incomplete phase  \n4. Honor open checkpoints (e.g. design not accepted)  \n\n## Switching agents\n\nBecause evidence is on disk:\n\n1. Install Praxis on the new agent (or use repo skills)  \n2. Open the same repository  \n3. Resume from `.workflows/{id}/`  \n\nDo not rely on the previous chat transcript.\n\n## Blocked phases\n\nIf `blocked`, the agent should state what unblocks (human decision, missing package, failing tests) and leave artifacts current.\n",
  "skills/catalog": "# Skills catalog\n\nPraxis ships **delivery workflows**, **support workflows**, and **embedded templates**.\n\n## Delivery\n\n| Skill | Purpose |\n|---|---|\n| `praxis-init` | Project direction and skill dependency gate |\n| `praxis-feature-flow` | Lifecycle orchestration + resume |\n| `praxis-refine` | Vague request → structured task |\n| `praxis-research` | AS-IS facts only |\n| `praxis-design` | Architecture, ADRs, contracts, challenge |\n| `praxis-plan` | Vertical phases + TDD criteria |\n| `praxis-implement` | One phase: write, review, gate |\n| `praxis-pr` | PR from artifacts |\n| `praxis-docs-suite` | Documentation suite |\n| `praxis-sentry-triage` | Sentry → grouped tasks |\n| `praxis-qa-checklist` | Coverage-driven QA lists |\n| `praxis-system-profile` | Actors, integrations, questions |\n| `praxis-skill-from-git` | History → project skill |\n| `praxis-ai-debug` | Install / package health |\n| `praxis-clear-speech` | Clear writing policy + audit |\n\n## Templates and references\n\n| Skill | Purpose |\n|---|---|\n| `praxis-adr-template` | One ADR per decision |\n| `praxis-api-contracts-template` | REST / async contracts |\n| `praxis-design-template` | Architecture / diagram format |\n| `praxis-owasp-top-10` | OWASP + modern threats |\n| `praxis-security-audit-checklist` | Security review checklist |\n| `praxis-stoplight-docs` | Stoplight / SMD docs |\n| `praxis-task-refinement` | INVEST, story formats |\n| `praxis-tdd-approach` | Phase TDD contract |\n| `praxis-test-design-techniques` | EP, BVA, tables, states |\n\n## Invocation\n\nCodex:\n\n```text\nUse $praxis-research to …\n```\n\nClaude Code (if installed): `/praxis-research`\n\nEach delivery skill has its own page in the sidebar.\n",
  "skills/praxis-init": "# `$praxis-init`\n\nInitialize, audit, confirm, or refresh project direction and optional external skill dependencies.\n\n## When to use\n\n- Starting work in a repository\n- Praxis context missing or unconfirmed\n- Direction, design routing, or skill sources changed\n\n## Writes\n\n- `.praxis/project.md`\n- Optional `.praxis/skills.yaml`\n- Managed block in root `AGENTS.md`\n\n## Procedure (agent)\n\n1. Detect new vs existing project\n2. Interview or audit\n3. Draft or refresh profile\n4. Set `needs-confirmation` until user confirms\n5. Validate size and schema\n6. Optionally draft skills.yaml candidates (never auto-install)\n7. Patch AGENTS.md discovery bridge\n\n## Human involvement\n\nYou must confirm the profile before agents treat it as final for mutations.\n\n## See also\n\n- [Skills catalog](/docs/skills/catalog)\n- [Feature flow](/docs/flow/overview)\n",
  "skills/praxis-feature-flow": "# `$praxis-feature-flow`\n\nCoordinate the complexity-adaptive feature lifecycle with resumable state under `.workflows/{id}/`.\n\n## When to use\n\n- Multi-phase delivery\n- Need status/resume across sessions\n- Adaptive ceremony\n\n## Writes\n\n- `.workflows/{feature-id}/state.json`\n- Phase directories for refine/research/design/plan/implement/docs/pr\n\n## Procedure (agent)\n\n1. Ensure project context when required\n2. Assess complexity; get path acceptance when needed\n3. Run frontend gate if visual work applies\n4. Execute phases; persist state\n5. Stop at checkpoints\n6. Support status and resume\n\n## Human involvement\n\nDesign acceptance and ship remain human decisions on non-trivial work.\n\n## See also\n\n- [Skills catalog](/docs/skills/catalog)\n- [Feature flow](/docs/flow/overview)\n",
  "skills/praxis-refine": "# `$praxis-refine`\n\nTurn vague product or engineering requests into structured task contracts.\n\n## When to use\n\n- Unclear asks from PM or stakeholders\n- Need stories, AC, risks, estimate before design\n\n## Writes\n\n- Refined task artifact under the feature workflow (or standalone path)\n\n## Procedure (agent)\n\n1. Load task-refinement references as needed\n2. Clarify only blocking unknowns\n3. Write user stories / AC / risks / sizing\n4. Do not design solutions yet\n\n## Human involvement\n\nReview the refined task before large design investment.\n\n## See also\n\n- [Skills catalog](/docs/skills/catalog)\n- [Feature flow](/docs/flow/overview)\n",
  "skills/praxis-research": "# `$praxis-research`\n\nProduce facts-only AS-IS research before proposing a solution.\n\n## When to use\n\n- Need codebase truth\n- Before design or risky change\n\n## Writes\n\n- Research dossier: facts, entrypoints, complexity notes\n\n## Procedure (agent)\n\n1. Load research rules\n2. Trace code and configs\n3. Record facts only (no redesign)\n4. List open questions\n5. Assess complexity\n\n## Human involvement\n\nChallenge incomplete or solution-shaped research.\n\n## See also\n\n- [Skills catalog](/docs/skills/catalog)\n- [Feature flow](/docs/flow/overview)\n",
  "skills/praxis-design": "# `$praxis-design`\n\nCreate architecture, diagrams, ADRs, API contracts, test strategy, and challenge review.\n\n## When to use\n\n- After research for non-trivial change\n- Before implementation of structural work\n\n## Writes\n\n- design/architecture.md, diagrams, adr/*, contracts\n\n## Procedure (agent)\n\n1. Complete frontend skill gate when applicable\n2. Draft architecture and ADRs\n3. Run challenge review as required\n4. Stop for human checkpoint\n\n## Human involvement\n\nDo not allow implement until design is accepted or explicitly waived.\n\n## See also\n\n- [Skills catalog](/docs/skills/catalog)\n- [Feature flow](/docs/flow/overview)\n",
  "skills/praxis-plan": "# `$praxis-plan`\n\nDecompose accepted design into vertical phases with TDD and verification criteria.\n\n## When to use\n\n- Design accepted\n- Need ordered implementation slices\n\n## Writes\n\n- plan/overview.md, plan/phase-N.md\n\n## Procedure (agent)\n\n1. Read design artifacts\n2. Slice vertical phases\n3. Map dependencies\n4. Attach verification / TDD criteria per phase\n\n## Human involvement\n\nConfirm phase boundaries if they affect release planning.\n\n## See also\n\n- [Skills catalog](/docs/skills/catalog)\n- [Feature flow](/docs/flow/overview)\n",
  "skills/praxis-implement": "# `$praxis-implement`\n\nImplement one planned phase with writer, reviewer, and quality-gate responsibilities.\n\n## When to use\n\n- Phase plan ready\n- Scope clear\n\n## Writes\n\n- Code + tests + implement reports / review notes\n\n## Procedure (agent)\n\n1. Lock scope to the phase\n2. Load primary visual skill when UI applies\n3. TDD-oriented changes\n4. Reviewer / quality-gate pass\n5. Write phase report\n\n## Human involvement\n\nReject silent scope expansion into later phases.\n\n## See also\n\n- [Skills catalog](/docs/skills/catalog)\n- [Feature flow](/docs/flow/overview)\n",
  "skills/praxis-pr": "# `$praxis-pr`\n\nPrepare or create a pull request from workflow artifacts, not chat memory.\n\n## When to use\n\n- Implementation evidence ready\n- Need reviewable PR\n\n## Writes\n\n- PR summary, test plan, links to design/research\n\n## Procedure (agent)\n\n1. Collect diffs, reports, CI signals\n2. Draft PR body from artifacts\n3. Open draft or ready PR as asked\n\n## Human involvement\n\nMerge remains a human (or org policy) decision.\n\n## See also\n\n- [Skills catalog](/docs/skills/catalog)\n- [Feature flow](/docs/flow/overview)\n",
  "skills/praxis-docs-suite": "# `$praxis-docs-suite`\n\nGenerate or update technical facts, architecture, OpenAPI, feature docs, and indexes.\n\n## When to use\n\n- Docs suite missing or stale\n- After significant product change\n\n## Writes\n\n- docs tree, OpenAPI, .meta.json as applicable\n\n## Procedure (agent)\n\n1. Inventory code and existing docs\n2. Update facts and API surfaces\n3. Cross-review packaging when required\n\n## Human involvement\n\nReview published docs for accuracy before release notes.\n\n## See also\n\n- [Skills catalog](/docs/skills/catalog)\n- [Feature flow](/docs/flow/overview)\n",
  "skills/praxis-sentry-triage": "# `$praxis-sentry-triage`\n\nGroup Sentry issues into actionable tasks that feed refine/feature flow.\n\n## When to use\n\n- Noisy production errors\n- Need prioritized engineering work\n\n## Writes\n\n- Triage packets / grouped issue docs\n\n## Procedure (agent)\n\n1. Pull recent issues (CLI/API/MCP as available)\n2. Cluster by root cause\n3. Assign severity\n4. Write groups for refine\n\n## Human involvement\n\nConfirm P0 before large interrupts.\n\n## See also\n\n- [Skills catalog](/docs/skills/catalog)\n- [Feature flow](/docs/flow/overview)\n",
  "skills/praxis-qa-checklist": "# `$praxis-qa-checklist`\n\nGenerate structured QA checklists from features or artifacts using test design techniques.\n\n## When to use\n\n- Need coverage-driven checklist\n- Before or after implement\n\n## Writes\n\n- QA checklist markdown\n\n## Procedure (agent)\n\n1. Load test design techniques\n2. Apply EP/BVA/tables/states as fit\n3. Write checklist with priorities\n\n## Human involvement\n\nAdjust critical path cases for release criteria.\n\n## See also\n\n- [Skills catalog](/docs/skills/catalog)\n- [Feature flow](/docs/flow/overview)\n",
  "skills/praxis-system-profile": "# `$praxis-system-profile`\n\nDescribe actors, use cases, integrations, data flows, issues, and open questions.\n\n## When to use\n\n- Integration landscape unclear\n- Onboarding a complex subsystem\n\n## Writes\n\n- System profile document\n\n## Procedure (agent)\n\n1. Trace integrations and actors\n2. Map flows\n3. List issues and open questions\n\n## Human involvement\n\nUse to align stakeholders before big design.\n\n## See also\n\n- [Skills catalog](/docs/skills/catalog)\n- [Feature flow](/docs/flow/overview)\n",
  "skills/praxis-skill-from-git": "# `$praxis-skill-from-git`\n\nExtract real repository conventions from Git history into a project skill.\n\n## When to use\n\n- Want project-specific patterns grounded in history\n- Not a generic style guide\n\n## Writes\n\n- `.agents/skills/{project}-patterns/SKILL.md`\n\n## Procedure (agent)\n\n1. Sample history\n2. Distill conventions with evidence\n3. Write skill package\n\n## Human involvement\n\nReview generated skill before requiring it on the team.\n\n## See also\n\n- [Skills catalog](/docs/skills/catalog)\n- [Feature flow](/docs/flow/overview)\n",
  "skills/praxis-ai-debug": "# `$praxis-ai-debug`\n\nInspect package, skill, reference, MCP, installation, and workflow health.\n\n## When to use\n\n- Skill missing in session\n- Install or discovery issues\n\n## Writes\n\n- Status notes; no mandatory mutation\n\n## Procedure (agent)\n\n1. Check install receipts and skill paths\n2. Compare agent homes\n3. Report root cause and fix steps\n\n## Human involvement\n\nUsually restart agent after install fixes.\n\n## See also\n\n- [Skills catalog](/docs/skills/catalog)\n- [Feature flow](/docs/flow/overview)\n",
  "skills/praxis-clear-speech": "# `$praxis-clear-speech`\n\nWrite or audit clear replies, technical text, code messages, and UI copy.\n\n## When to use\n\n- Need clear operator-facing text\n- Audit docs or messages\n\n## Writes\n\n- Revised text; optional audit report\n\n## Procedure (agent)\n\n1. Load policy for project mode\n2. Protect identifiers\n3. Rewrite or audit\n4. Optional structural script\n\n## Human involvement\n\nSee [Clear Speech concept](/docs/concepts/clear-speech).\n\n## See also\n\n- [Skills catalog](/docs/skills/catalog)\n- [Feature flow](/docs/flow/overview)\n",
  "skills/templates": "# Templates and references\n\nEmbedded skills used by design, security, docs, and planning agents.\n\n| Skill | Use |\n|---|---|\n| `praxis-adr-template` | One-file ADR contract |\n| `praxis-api-contracts-template` | REST and async message formats |\n| `praxis-design-template` | Architecture + diagram structure |\n| `praxis-owasp-top-10` | Vulnerability patterns by tech |\n| `praxis-security-audit-checklist` | Security review checklist |\n| `praxis-stoplight-docs` | Stoplight/SMD guidance |\n| `praxis-task-refinement` | INVEST, stories, sizing |\n| `praxis-tdd-approach` | Phase TDD sections |\n| `praxis-test-design-techniques` | EP, BVA, decision tables, states, pairwise |\n\nThese are not full delivery orchestrators. Delivery skills load them when needed.\n",
  "cli/overview": "# CLI overview\n\nBinary: `praxis-skills` (via `npx praxis-skills@beta`)\n\nZero runtime dependencies. Node 22+.\n\n## Commands\n\n| Command | Purpose |\n|---|---|\n| `install` | Install skills (and optional Taste family) |\n| `doctor` | Verify installed skills (and Taste if receipt says so) |\n| `uninstall` | Remove Praxis-owned installs |\n| `detect` | Detect agent homes |\n| `list` | List packaged skill names |\n| `version` | Package version |\n\n## Ownership\n\nThe CLI only mutates paths owned by `distribution/manifest.json` (and Taste paths when you opted in). Unrelated skills are preserved.\n\n## Next\n\n- [install](/docs/cli/install)\n- [doctor · detect · list](/docs/cli/doctor)\n",
  "cli/install": "# CLI: install\n\n```bash\npraxis-skills install\npraxis-skills install --user | --repo [path] | --target <skills-dir>\n                      [--agents <id,id|all>] [--all-agents]\n                      [--with-slash-commands | --no-slash-commands]\n                      [--with-taste-skill | --no-taste-skill]\n                      [--commands-target <dir>]\n                      [--force] [--dry-run] [--yes] [--json]\n```\n\n## Interactive default\n\nOn a TTY with no target flags, the guided wizard runs:\n\n1. Scope: user vs repo  \n2. Agents: multi-select  \n3. Taste Skill family: **default no**  \n4. Plan + confirm  \n\n## Non-interactive\n\nWithout `--agents`, installs **Codex only** (backward compatible).\n\n```bash\nnpx praxis-skills@beta install --user --yes\nnpx praxis-skills@beta install --user --agents codex,claude-code --yes\nnpx praxis-skills@beta install --user --with-taste-skill --force --yes\n```\n\n## Replace policy\n\nExisting Praxis skill directories are **skipped** unless `--force`. Force needs confirm or `--yes`.\n\n## Receipts\n\nWrites install receipt (e.g. `praxis-skills.json`) under the agent root when applicable, including optional `tasteSkill` metadata.\n",
  "cli/doctor": "# CLI: doctor · detect · list · version\n\n## doctor\n\n```bash\nnpx praxis-skills@beta doctor --user\nnpx praxis-skills@beta doctor --user --agents codex,claude-code --json\n```\n\nChecks each expected Praxis skill `SKILL.md`. If a receipt claims Taste Skill was installed, verifies the Taste family too.\n\nExit code 1 when unhealthy.\n\n## detect\n\n```bash\nnpx praxis-skills@beta detect\nnpx praxis-skills@beta detect --json\n```\n\nFilesystem detection of agent homes. No install.\n\n## list\n\n```bash\nnpx praxis-skills@beta list --json\n```\n\nExact skill names owned by the distribution manifest.\n\n## version\n\n```bash\nnpx praxis-skills@beta version\n```\n",
  "cli/uninstall": "# CLI: uninstall\n\n```bash\nnpx praxis-skills@beta uninstall --user --yes\nnpx praxis-skills@beta uninstall --user --agents claude-code --dry-run\nnpx praxis-skills@beta uninstall --repo . --agents codex --yes\n```\n\nRemoves:\n\n- Praxis skill directories from the manifest (and legacy names when present)\n- Slash adapters Praxis owns\n- Install receipt when applicable\n\nDoes **not** delete unrelated skills. Prefer `--dry-run` first on multi-agent machines.\n\nProject files (`.praxis/`, `.workflows/`) are **not** removed by uninstall.\n",
  "cli/taste-skill": "# CLI: Taste Skill flag\n\n## Flag\n\n| Flag | Default | Meaning |\n|---|---|---|\n| `--with-taste-skill` | off | Install full pinned Taste family into each selected agent skills root |\n| `--no-taste-skill` | (explicit off) | Skip |\n\nWizard asks with default **no**.\n\n## Mechanism\n\n1. Read `distribution/taste-skill.json`  \n2. `git clone` + checkout pinned revision  \n3. Copy each `skills/{folder}` to install name directory  \n4. Write `praxis-taste-skill.json` pin note when agent root exists  \n5. Record `tasteSkill` on install receipt  \n\nRequires **git** on PATH.\n\n## Doctor\n\nTaste checks run only when `receipt.tasteSkill.installed` is true.\n\n## Policy reminder\n\nMissing Taste Skill must not block workflows. Present applicable skills must be used. See [Taste Skill routing](/docs/concepts/taste-skill).\n",
  "config/project-md": "# Configuration: project.md\n\nPath: `.praxis/project.md`\n\n## Frontmatter (typical)\n\n```yaml\n---\nschema: praxis-project/v1\nstatus: needs-confirmation # or confirmed\nproject_id: my-project\nproject_type: new # or existing\nsource: interview # audit | refresh\nvisual_scope: none # limited | significant\nclear_speech: default # strict | off\nupdated: YYYY-MM-DD\n---\n```\n\n## Body sections\n\n- Core Contract (compact)  \n- Project Concept  \n- Product Direction  \n- Experience Direction  \n- Communication Profile  \n- Design Skill Routing  \n- Reference Designs and Projects  \n- Existing System and Assets  \n- Constraints and Non-Negotiables  \n- Open Questions  \n- Confirmation  \n\n## Design skill routing\n\nOne primary visual skill or `none`. Supplements listed separately. Conflicting style primaries prohibited.\n\n## Validation\n\nRun the init validator script. Enforce word limits. Record SHA-256 in workflow state.\n\nSee [Project context](/docs/concepts/project-context).\n",
  "config/skills-yaml": "# Configuration: skills.yaml\n\nPath: `.praxis/skills.yaml` (optional)\n\n## Schema\n\n`schema: praxis-skills/v1`\n\n## Package fields\n\n| Field | Rule |\n|---|---|\n| `id` | Unique kebab-case |\n| `requirement` | `required` or `recommended` only |\n| `role` | Unique project responsibility |\n| `source.type` | git / marketplace / website / local-generation |\n| `source.url` | HTTPS when applicable |\n| `source.revision` | Pinned; no floating branches (`main`, `latest`) |\n| `skills` | Entrypoints only |\n| `rationale` | Why required |\n| `applies_when` | When to check |\n| `overflow_justification` | After fifth required package |\n\n## Runtime\n\n- Validate + hash with project context  \n- Never auto-install  \n- Missing required → block only affected work after consent path  \n- Missing recommended → report, continue  \n\n## Example: pin Taste Skill (frontend projects)\n\n```yaml\nschema: praxis-skills/v1\n\npackages:\n  - id: leonxlnx-taste-skill\n    requirement: recommended\n    role: primary-frontend-direction\n    source:\n      type: git\n      url: https://github.com/Leonxlnx/taste-skill\n      revision: e988add20dab0fa97d7a76781c48961c8184288e\n    skills:\n      - design-taste-frontend\n    rationale: Default visual direction for marketing and redesign (Taste Skill v2 experimental).\n    applies_when: Visually significant frontend design or implementation is in scope.\n```\n\nKeep the revision in sync with Praxis pin when possible: [distribution/taste-skill.json](https://github.com/EdwyReed/praxis-skills/blob/master/distribution/taste-skill.json).\n\n## Template in the package\n\nScaffold comments live in:\n\n- [plugin/skills/praxis-init/assets/skills-template.yaml](https://github.com/EdwyReed/praxis-skills/blob/master/plugin/skills/praxis-init/assets/skills-template.yaml)\n\n## Related\n\n- [Project context](/docs/concepts/project-context)\n- [Taste Skill routing](/docs/concepts/taste-skill)\n",
  "config/agents-md": "# Configuration: AGENTS.md\n\nRoot `AGENTS.md` receives a **managed Praxis block** from `$praxis-init`.\n\n## Purpose\n\nMake project context discoverable in Codex when:\n\n- Praxis skills are not installed  \n- Session context is heavily loaded  \n\n## Behavior\n\n- Instructs agents to read `.praxis/project.md` before project-scoped work  \n- Notes `needs-confirmation` limits  \n- Mentions optional `.praxis/skills.yaml` without loading package lists eagerly  \n\n## Editing\n\nDo not hand-edit the managed markers if you rely on init refresh. Keep project-specific agent rules outside the managed block.\n",
  "config/mcp": "# Configuration: MCP\n\nMCP servers are **optional**. Skills should degrade when tools are missing.\n\n## Policy\n\nPraxis Skills can use Sentry, Context7, OpenAI Docs, GitHub, browser, and Stoplight-related tooling when those integrations are available. They are optional unless a specific workflow needs live external data.\n\nIf a dependency is missing, workflow skills should either:\n\n- use filesystem-only fallback behavior, or  \n- report the exact missing dependency and the artifact that cannot be produced.\n\n## Common connectors\n\n| Domain | Example | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| Errors | Sentry MCP | Useful for `$praxis-sentry-triage` |\n| Library docs | Context7 | Library API facts |\n| Vendor docs | Platform documentation MCPs | When coding against a vendor API |\n| Repo / issues | GitHub MCP | Optional; prefer local git when enough |\n\n## Codex configuration\n\nAdd MCP servers in your Codex configuration **without committing secrets**.\n\nExample skeleton (fill commands/URLs/secrets outside the repo):\n\n```toml\n# ~/.codex/config.toml (example)\n\nmodel = \"gpt-5.5\"\nmodel_reasoning_effort = \"medium\"\n\n[features]\n# Optional. Required only when a workflow explicitly asks Codex to use subagents.\nmulti_agent = true\n\n# [mcp_servers.sentry]\n# command = \"npx\"\n# args = [\"-y\", \"@sentry/mcp-server\"]\n\n# [mcp_servers.context7]\n# command = \"npx\"\n# args = [\"-y\", \"@upstash/context7-mcp\"]\n\n# [mcp_servers.openaiDeveloperDocs]\n# url = \"https://developers.openai.com/mcp\"\n```\n\nSource example in the package:\n\n- [`.codex/config.example.toml`](https://github.com/EdwyReed/praxis-skills/blob/master/.codex/config.example.toml)\n\n## Guidance for agents\n\n1. Prefer repository files and local search first  \n2. Use MCP when it improves factual accuracy  \n3. Record when a tool was unavailable and how you worked around it  \n\n## Related\n\n- [`$praxis-sentry-triage`](/docs/skills/praxis-sentry-triage)\n- [`$praxis-ai-debug`](/docs/skills/praxis-ai-debug)\n- Package how-to: [docs/how/configure-mcp.md](https://github.com/EdwyReed/praxis-skills/blob/master/docs/how/configure-mcp.md)\n",
  "guides/first-feature": "# Guide: first feature\n\n## Goal\n\nShip one small-to-medium feature with Praxis artifacts and checkpoints.\n\n## Steps\n\n1. **Install** Praxis on your agent (Codex recommended).  \n2. **Init** project context; confirm `.praxis/project.md`.  \n3. **Feature flow** (or refine → research manually).  \n4. Accept complexity path.  \n5. Complete research; challenge solutions in research.  \n6. Design; **you** accept or amend.  \n7. Plan phases.  \n8. Implement **one** phase; run tests.  \n9. PR from artifacts.  \n10. Merge when satisfied.\n\n## Tips\n\n- Name skills explicitly in prompts  \n- Commit workflow artifacts that carry decisions  \n- Restart agent after install  \n- Prefer resume over re-explaining chat history  \n\n## Next\n\n- [Quick start](/docs/get-started/quick-start)\n- [Feature flow](/docs/flow/overview)\n",
  "guides/frontend": "# Guide: frontend work\n\n## Checklist\n\n1. Confirm `visual_scope` in project.md  \n2. Select one primary visual skill (often `design-taste-frontend`)  \n3. If missing, agent offers Taste install; missing does **not** block non-visual prep  \n4. Load the skill before visual design/code  \n5. Record selection in state/design/plan  \n6. Keep technical skills as supplements only  \n\n## Install Taste with Praxis\n\n```bash\nnpx praxis-skills@beta install --user --with-taste-skill --yes\n```\n\n## Out of Taste scope\n\nDashboards, dense admin, games: do not force Taste. Use product design system + engineering skills.\n\n## See\n\n- [Taste Skill routing](/docs/concepts/taste-skill)\n- [$praxis-design](/docs/skills/praxis-design)\n",
  "guides/migrate-claude": "# Guide: migrate from Claude Code surfaces\n\nThe original workflow source used Claude Code slash commands and install symlinks into `~/.claude`. That historical checkout installer is obsolete.\n\nPraxis is Codex-first. Claude support is install-time packaging:\n\n- full skill packages under `~/.claude/skills/praxis-*` (or project `.claude/skills`)\n- thin slash adapters under `commands/` as **`/praxis-*`**\n\n## Install Claude surface\n\n```bash\nnpx praxis-skills@beta install --user --agents claude-code --yes\n# interactive:\nnpx praxis-skills@beta install --user\n```\n\nCodex in parallel:\n\n```bash\nnpx praxis-skills@beta install --user --agents codex,claude-code --yes\n```\n\n## Command map\n\n| Slash command (prefixed) | Praxis skill (source of truth) |\n|---|---|\n| `/praxis-init` | `praxis-init` |\n| `/praxis-feature` | `praxis-feature-flow` |\n| `/praxis-refine` | `praxis-refine` |\n| `/praxis-research` | `praxis-research` |\n| `/praxis-design` | `praxis-design` |\n| `/praxis-plan` | `praxis-plan` |\n| `/praxis-implement` | `praxis-implement` |\n| `/praxis-docs-suite` | `praxis-docs-suite` |\n| `/praxis-pr` | `praxis-pr` |\n| `/praxis-sentry-triage` | `praxis-sentry-triage` |\n| `/praxis-qa-checklist` | `praxis-qa-checklist` |\n| `/praxis-system-profile` | `praxis-system-profile` |\n| `/praxis-skill-from-git` | `praxis-skill-from-git` |\n| `/praxis-ai-debug` | `praxis-ai-debug` |\n| `/praxis-clear-speech` | `praxis-clear-speech` |\n\nUnprefixed names (`/init`, `/feature`, …) are **not** installed: they collide with Claude built-ins. The installer removes those legacy adapters when present.\n\n## Rules\n\n1. Prefer `/praxis-init` over bare `/init`  \n2. Slash commands do **not** re-implement workflows; they load the skill package  \n3. Codex skill invocation (`$praxis-*`) stays first-class  \n4. Keep `.praxis/` and `.workflows/` as the shared truth across agents  \n5. Claude Agent Teams map to optional subagents; if unavailable, skills run roles inline  \n\n## Surface comparison\n\n| Concern | Claude-era source | Codex-native port |\n|---|---|---|\n| Entry point | Slash commands in `commands/` | Skills in `.agents/skills/` |\n| Durable guidance | `CLAUDE.md` | `AGENTS.md` |\n| Agent roles | `agents/**/*.md` | `references/agents/**/*.md` |\n| Multi-agent work | Agent Teams | Optional subagents + inline fallback |\n| Install path | `~/.claude` symlinks | Repo / user skills / plugin |\n| Distribution | Git checkout + symlinks | npm CLI + plugin bundle |\n\n## Source docs in the package\n\n- [docs/how/migrate-from-claude-code.md](https://github.com/EdwyReed/praxis-skills/blob/master/docs/how/migrate-from-claude-code.md)\n- [docs/comparisons/claude-code-vs-codex-surfaces.md](https://github.com/EdwyReed/praxis-skills/blob/master/docs/comparisons/claude-code-vs-codex-surfaces.md)\n\n## Related\n\n- [Agents](/docs/get-started/agents)\n- [Installation](/docs/get-started/installation)\n",
  "guides/uninstall": "# Guide: uninstall\n\n```bash\nnpx praxis-skills@beta uninstall --user --yes\nnpx praxis-skills@beta uninstall --repo . --agents codex,claude-code --yes\n```\n\n## What remains\n\n- Your `.praxis/` and `.workflows/` project files (not removed by uninstall)  \n- Unrelated skills in the same home  \n\nDelete project Praxis files manually if you want a full cleanse (careful: project data).\n\n## Taste Skill\n\nIf you installed Taste via `--with-taste-skill`, those install-name directories may still exist under the agent skills root. Remove them explicitly if you no longer want them.\n",
}
